guide='''<main class="pe-page ui-guide"><div class="container"><div class="pe-section-head"><p>Oanarina UI Tool · Mac preview</p><h1>From blank canvas to first screen.</h1><p class="pe-section-sub">A practical guide to the tools that work in version 0.1.0.</p></div><article><h2>1. Begin with a file</h2><p>Open the Mac app and explore the editable sample. Click the home icon for recent files, a fresh design or an existing .oui project. The browser and native app keep their own local recovery stores.</p><img src="images/apps/ui-tool/home.png" alt="Oanarina UI Tool recent files and starter choices"></article><article><h2>2. Draw and select</h2><p>Use <kbd>F</kbd> for frames, <kbd>R</kbd> for rectangles, <kbd>O</kbd> for ellipses, <kbd>L</kbd> for lines, <kbd>Shift L</kbd> for arrows and <kbd>T</kbd> for text. The shape dropdown includes stars and polygons. <kbd>P</kbd> draws straight pen segments; Enter finishes. <kbd>Shift P</kbd> is freehand pencil.</p><p><kbd>V</kbd> selects and moves. Shift-click selects several layers. Drag a blank region for a marquee. Use the hierarchical layer tree to choose nested layers, hide or lock them. Hold Space and drag to pan; Command-scroll zooms around your pointer.</p></article><article><h2>3. Refine properties and type</h2><p>Select a layer and edit coordinates, dimensions, angle, radius, fill, stroke and typography in the inspector. Double-click text to edit it. In Typography, choose Browse Google &amp; Mac fonts to search the 1,959-family catalog. Preview a font and apply it. Twenty-four bundled families work offline; others download and cache. Installed commercial fonts are listed only in the native Mac app.</p><p>Rich text, italics, automatic paragraph wrapping and full variable-axis controls are still planned.</p></article><article><h2>4. Arrange a layout</h2><p>Command-G groups; Command-Shift-G ungroups. Command-D duplicates. Object and Arrange menus expose components, ordering, alignment and distribution. Containers support basic Row, Stack and fixed-column Grid layout, with gap and uniform padding. Responsive constraints, wrap, hug/fill sizing, variants and live component propagation are not complete.</p></article><article><h2>5. Preview and leave a note</h2><p>In Prototype, give a layer a destination frame. Present and click the layer to navigate. Use the previous/next buttons to browse frames. This is simple click-through navigation, without animation or conditional state. Press C and click the canvas for a local note; View → Comments lets you resolve or reopen it.</p></article><article><h2>6. Save and export</h2><p>Command-S saves an editable .oui; Command-Shift-S saves a separate copy. Browser saves download a file; the Mac app uses native file dialogs and atomic writes. Recovery and recent files are local and quota limited. File → Save a named version stores a local checkpoint. Command-Z and Command-Shift-Z undo and redo.</p><p>Select layers or a frame, then export SVG, PNG or JPEG at 1×–4×. With nothing selected, the current page is exported. SVG imports as one visual asset. Save .oui to preserve editable layer structure.</p></article><article><h2>7. Transfer to and from Figma</h2><p>Download <a href="downloads/ui-tool/figma-bridge.zip" download>Figma Bridge</a> and unzip it. In Figma desktop, choose Plugins → Development → Import plugin from manifest and choose manifest.json. Run Oanarina Bridge. Export selected layers, the current page or all pages as .oui, then open the file in Oanarina. To go back, save/export .oui and import through the plugin.</p><p>Frames, shapes, simple text, solid fills, basic strokes and raster images have transfer paths. Advanced effects, text ranges, variants, linkage, layout sizing and prototypes are reduced or omitted. Read the report and inspect the result. Automated API-mock tests pass; the real plugin round trip still needs validation. Binary .fig files are not supported.</p></article><article><h2>8. Find a command or check the plan</h2><p>Command-K searches available actions. Help → Keyboard shortcuts lists this build’s shortcuts. Help → Feature register provides all 1,860 requirements and their status. Planned and partial requirements are not promises of completed functionality.</p><p><a href="ui-tool.html">Return to UI Tool &amp; downloads →</a></p></article></div></main>'''
(site/'ui-tool-guide.html').write_text(head.replace('Oanarina UI Tool — Interface Design for Mac','Oanarina UI Tool User Guide').replace('https://www.oanarinaldi.com/ui-tool.html','https://www.oanarinaldi.com/ui-tool-guide.html')+header+guide+footer)
privacy='''<main class="pe-page ui-guide"><div class="container"><div class="pe-section-head"><p>Oanarina UI Tool</p><h1>Privacy &amp; your files</h1><p>October 29, 2026 · version 0.1.0</p></div><article><h2>Local editing</h2><p>The preview does not require an account, upload your design to a server, or include app analytics. Projects you explicitly save stay at the destination you choose. Recovery copies, recent files, comments and snapshots are stored on this device, subject to browser storage limits.</p><h2>Local resource server</h2><p>The native Mac app serves its bundled public editor files only on 127.0.0.1:51981. User project files are not served by that HTTP server. The native bridge handles only the app’s main-frame requests.</p><h2>Google Fonts</h2><p>Twenty-four font families are bundled. If you preview or apply another family, the app contacts fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com. Those services receive the normal network request, including your IP address and the requested font. The app does not send your design text as a font-subsetting request. Downloaded font data is cached locally.</p><h2>Installed fonts</h2><p>The native picker reads installed font family names through macOS. It does not copy proprietary font files into projects. Use fonts under their own licenses.</p><h2>Figma Bridge</h2><p>The development plugin exchanges .oui files you choose and requires no network access itself. Figma’s own service and policies apply when you run it there. Import/export may create new pages in the Figma file you have open.</p><h2>Your control</h2><p>Export .oui for a portable backup. Remove local browser/site data to clear recovery, local histories and downloaded-font caches; save important projects first. Files you explicitly exported are managed separately through Finder.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For questions or feedback, use the <a href="index.html#contact">contact page</a>. <a href="ui-tool.html">Return to UI Tool</a>.</p></article></div></main>'''
(site/'ui-tool-privacy.html').write_text(head.replace('Oanarina UI Tool — Interface Design for Mac','Oanarina UI Tool Privacy').replace('https://www.oanarinaldi.com/ui-tool.html','https://www.oanarinaldi.com/ui-tool-privacy.html')+header+privacy+footer)
